commit ebd8b0ba54823fe326a85ec3acc4309990b715c6
Author: clever-wolf-203 <clever-wolf-203@invalid>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 17:39:13 2026 +0000

    prep: a ReleaseLocus record carries revision+spine+locus to one install (pure refactor)
    
    deploy-intent-owns-artifact-closure preparatory PR for the artifact-closure gate.
    
    - ONE function mints a ReleaseLocus record from (base_root, revision), carrying revision,
      spine and the locus directory together (release_locus_record). The install now takes that
      record and NO separate revision argument, so a locus cannot be paired with a revision it
      was not minted for (review 95699; gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed: making a wrong state
      unwritable beats catching it).
    - EXACTLY ONE install function: the pass-through approval_broker_tree_install wrapper is
      folded into the install and the _at variant deleted. Every caller (live_deploy broker_tree
      port, dark_stage_broker_tree, microvm controller tree step, the two install witnesses) mints
      the record via release_locus_record and calls the one install; nothing re-derives the locus.
    - dark_helper_snapshot_at / dark_helper_verify_at take the computed dir as a required arg
      (stop deriving helper_locus_dir internally); live_deploy_apply_root_helper_snapshot_on_host
      takes dir and its 2 port callers (live_deploy, fleet board_function_converge) compute via
      helper_locus_dir. dark_helper_retire_at unchanged (operates on locus.base).
    - No behavior change: every caller writes to the same place it did before, only now the place
      is carried on one record that the caller mints.
    
    Node: node://adhoc-3e6e9bfb-d59 (rn_Z0G9G30XDNQJG7QYJ0M6NAVY0T)

